# Frozen wire-equivalence hashes for the builtin native documents.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-21: the multicast route's schema declares the lock-anchor
# trio, and the wire digest covers declared keys even when absent, so the
# 5.15 multicast profile's bytes changed while no value did.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-25: kernelsnitch.mm_struct_sz returned to the profile
# schema (written only from a measurement), so the digest covers the declared
# key again and every document's bytes changed; no bundled value did.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-27: the bundled profiles carry their measured/known
# mm_struct stride (5.10 = 960, 5.15/6.1 = 1024, 6.6/6.12 = 1280; the
# 6.x values are QEMU-confirmed and replace the null/default).
# Re-frozen 2026-10-29: stage-3 layout facts (cred usage/uid/security,
# rt_mutex_size, waiter_layout) entered the wire schema. They are absent
# on the bundled profiles, so no value changed, but the digest covers
# every declared key and every document's bytes changed.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-29 (bundle fix): the 6.1 profiles take the BTF cred
# values from credential-6_1.conf (copy 128, caps 40); the 5.15 profiles
# keep the 5.x template block (copy 176, caps 48, four reference slots).
# Their bytes still carry the declared stage-3 keys, absent on both.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-30: page-free Stage 1 added the `selinux` (enforcing,
# initialized) and `w1_scratch` (image) wire sections. They are absent on
# the bundled profiles, so no value changed, but the digest covers every
# declared key and every document's bytes changed; the schema digest moved
# to 0x28706e4538054d46.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-30 (Stage 4): the eight bundled 5.10 profiles carry the
# page-free blocks -- `selinux` (enforcing 0, initialized 2) and `w1_scratch`
# (the in-anchor slot on 136/209/226/236; bm_pmd on 81/177/198; the Samsung
# array's zero gap on 101). Only those eight documents changed.
# Re-frozen 2026-10-31: the compat select carrier added three declared
# `route.select_stack` keys (compat_carrier, waiter_home, select_dst_depth).
# They are absent on every bundled profile, so no value changed, but the
# digest covers every declared key: only the select_stack documents' bytes
# moved (the sigreturn 5.10.81/101 documents are unchanged).
# Re-frozen 2026-11-01 (r8): the bundled diting 5.10.81/101 profiles now carry
# the compat select carrier (select_stack with compat_carrier, waiter_home,
# select_dst_depth) instead of the sigreturn route; only those two documents
# changed. 5.10.81 is device-proven (10/10); 5.10.101 remains a QEMU candidate.
# Re-frozen 2026-11-06 (xaga): the Redmi Note 11T Pro / POCO X4 GT profiles
# (5.10.66, 5.10.168-00002, 5.10.226-00047) entered the bundle. The measured
# mm_struct stride was restored on the four regenerated 5.10 assets; only
# 5.10.168-00001 is in this fixture, and its bytes moved (960, the value its
# QEMU dump measures). The other documents' bytes are unchanged.
# Re-frozen 2026-11-10 (anchor alignment): the two bundled anchors whose bases
# were 4-aligned now use the 8-aligned base with the usable prefix re-rounded
# to a stride multiple -- 5.15.194 47903572/4096 -> 47903576/4064 and
# 6.1.138-mi 36850380/4096 -> 36850384/4064 (the native refuses a misaligned
# anchor). Only those two documents changed; every other row is unchanged.
# Re-frozen 2026-11-10 (pipeline cross-check): `meta.pipeline` entered the
# wire schema (the app's resolved GhostLock/DirtyFrag choice). These golden
# documents are built without it (absent), so no value changed, but the
# digest covers every declared key and every document's bytes changed; the
# schema digest moved to 0x6d7228fbbf71e00c.
# Re-frozen 2026-11-14: the compat select carrier's `compat_futex_abi`
# entered the `route.select_stack` schema (the derived ABI for a home that is
# not the 5.x constants). It is absent on every bundled profile, so no value
# changed, but the digest covers every declared key and every document's bytes
# moved; the schema digest is now 0x275387e01fa41b2a.
# Re-frozen 2026-11-14 (fact sync): the bundled assets were synced to their store
# supersets -- waiter_layout blocks, route compact_waiter/compat ABI, the cred
# stage-3 fields (family includes), kernelsnitch rt_mutex_size, the offset null
# placeholders, the 6.1.157 selinux block -- and the 6.1.138-mi symbol offsets
# were corrected to the QEMU-witnessed store values (0x2C0 _text/_stext base).
# Wire bytes moved for every affected document; the only measured value change
# was the -mi pair.
# Re-frozen 2026-11-15 (tanzanite): the Redmi Note 14 4G 5.10.236 build
# (5.10.236-android12-9-00020-gf997514b333d-ab13743839) entered the bundle.
# One document added; every other row is unchanged.
# Re-frozen 2026-11-23: the 5.10.81-android12-9-00001-g6cd504626bae-ab8485363
# and 5.10.226-android12-9-00064-gea4a6f067d3f-ab12969919 assets regained the
# measured kernelsnitch.mm_struct_sz = 960 (the timer store sweep's check
# found them missing); only those two documents changed.
# Re-frozen 2026-11-24: the native input is the one rendered JSON
# document (the GLK1 wire is gone). Every row moved; no value did.
